# Digital Twin Agent — Irrigated Parcels

Build the **Agent Jumeaux Numériques** for the `intern` project. This agent manages a virtual replica of irrigated parcels, ingests sensor readings, computes irrigation recommendations via a physics-based model, and lets researchers run "what-if" simulation scenarios — all powered by Mistral AI for natural-language rationale generation.

## Scope

From the cahier de charge: *"synchronisation des jumeaux numériques (bassin versant, parcelles irriguées, réseaux hydrauliques)"*

For the MVP we focus on **irrigated parcels** — this is the most concrete domain and we already have a proven irrigation algorithm from the `internship` project that we can port. Bassin versant and réseaux hydrauliques can be added as extensions later.

## Reference Code

The `internship` project (Django) contains a working irrigation recommendation service in [services.py](file:///c:/Users/aziz/OneDrive/Bureau/internship/backend/lab/services.py) and data models in [models.py](file:///c:/Users/aziz/OneDrive/Bureau/internship/backend/lab/models.py). We will **port the science** (the `calculate_irrigation_recommendation` function) into the FastAPI/async architecture of the `intern` project.

