### 3. Backend — Services (the science)

#### [NEW] [irrigation.py](file:///c:/Users/aziz/OneDrive/Bureau/intern/agents/digitaltwin/services/irrigation.py)

Port the `calculate_irrigation_recommendation` function from the `internship` project. This is a **physics-based water balance model**:
- Input: soil moisture, field capacity, wilting point, rainfall, evapotranspiration, crop coefficient
- Output: water balance, recommended irrigation (mm), confidence score, text rationale
- Crop coefficients for: wheat (0.95), olive (0.65), citrus (0.85), vegetable (1.05), forage (1.10)

#### [NEW] [simulator.py](file:///c:/Users/aziz/OneDrive/Bureau/intern/agents/digitaltwin/services/simulator.py)

Simulation engine that runs "what-if" scenarios on the irrigation model:
- Takes a parcel + modifier (e.g. `rainfall_factor: 0.7` = 30% less rain)
- Runs the irrigation model with modified inputs
- Uses Mistral AI to generate a natural-language analysis comparing baseline vs. modified scenario

---

### 4. Backend — Agent

#### [NEW] [agent.py](file:///c:/Users/aziz/OneDrive/Bureau/intern/agents/digitaltwin/agent.py)

`DigitalTwinAgent(BaseAgent)` with methods:
- `ingest_reading(parcel_id, reading_data)` — store sensor reading + auto-generate recommendation if soil moisture is below threshold
- `generate_recommendation(parcel_id)` — compute irrigation advice from latest reading
- `run_simulation(parcel_id, scenario)` — execute a what-if scenario

